In article <01bcabf2$ed346300$e93631cc@destin.emeraldcoast.com>, "Phillip Destin" <destin@emeraldcoast.com> writes:
>Hi: 
>
>I am trying to display an xterm from a Sun to an Alpha 
>running OpenVMS 6.2 and UCX 3.3.  On the Alpha, I enable
>the RLOGIN service and set the node, username, and 
>transport fields in the Session Manager..Options..Security.
First set username * (wildcard) and try it (username is not used for TCPIP).

To check if it's really a security access problem, 
wildcard node, username and transport: * * *
That disables all security access checks and you can see if the problem persists.
Then you may try to tigthen the access to one node, leaving username and transport wildcarded.
But beware of cache and deferral effects. If one combination works and you tigthen the access
and retry, the system may still use the old values! 


