Then of course there is always leap year calculations.  The simple function that
is always seen is
something along the following:

int
check_leap_year( int test_year )
{
    return ( ( ( (test_year % 4) == 0 ) && ( (test_year % 100) != 0 ) ) ||
                    ( (test_year % 400) == 0 ) );
}

Note that this function fails to work when called as:

        check_leap_year( my_tm_struct.tm_year )

Also you probably want to write a simple test program
to check your OS's C library functions.  Several OS's
until very recently still shipped with non-compliant
date related library functions.

So in answer to your question, while grep is a good place
to start, you will still need to take a hard look at the code.

John Kroll




