David Means wrote:
> If you're greping through 1000's of lines of ( C/C++ ) code for date related
> bugs, what do you look for?  My first assumption is to find tm_year.
> 
> What other stuff do you look for?

It is matter of how sure you want to be:

1)  Search for year and f.ex. a dozen other suspect strings and inspect
    the found locations manually. You will find most problem spots.

2)  Inspect all code modules using time manually. You wil find almost
    all problem spots.

3)  Inspect everything manually. You wil find everything (assuming
    actually done carefully).

So grep'ing is taking a chance, but if your cost-benefit analysis says,
that is the way to go, then ...

Other good strings to search for that come to my mind is:
gmtime,localtime,asciitime,ctime,strftime. But ask your
programmers what they usually use for year, if they often use f.ex. yy,
then add that to the list.

