You might find that converting the proxy database again is the solution. 
If your local namespace was not correctly configured when the conversion
first ran you will now have a combination of converted and unconverted
entries in the database.

It's a while since I explicitly converted a proxy database using
SYS$SYSTEM:CONVERT_PROXY, but I seem to recall there are some traps waiting
for the unwary, for example if NET$PROXY isn't defined and there is a
SYS$SPECIFIC:[SYSEXE]NET$PROXY.DAT then the conversion doesn't work
properly.  I also can't remember whether it's necessary to restart the
security server or not.
